# make - GNU make
dev-build/make static -nls

# gdb — target-native debugger, runs ON the i486 disc (not a cross-host
# debugger). PROJECT DOCTRINE: Python is excluded from this image, so
# -python is mandatory here regardless of upstream's +python default.
# +server: ships gdbserver too — small, standalone, and NOT disabled by the
# ebuild's is_cross() cross-check (this build's CTARGET defaults to CHOST,
# so is_cross() is false here, same as every other world package).
# +xml: parses gdbserver's XML target-description/memory-map exchange and
# syscall-catchpoint tables; pulls dev-libs/expat, a small new dep (see
# report §3). +lzma: reads LZMA-compressed separate debuginfo; free, since
# app-arch/xz-utils is already a static world package. Everything else is
# left at the global USE="-*" default (off): -debuginfod avoids a new
# dev-libs/elfutils dep for a live disc with no debuginfod server to talk
# to; -guile/-source-highlight/-babeltrace/-rocm avoid heavy optional
# scripting/highlighting/GPU-tracing deps; -multitarget/-cet/-zstd/-xxhash/
# -sim/-test/-vanilla are pure minimalism calls (see report §2 table).
# "static" kept for documentation parity though this ebuild has no
# IUSE=static of its own (static linking comes from the repo-wide
# package.env static.conf catch-all, same as ethtool/hdparm/etc. above).
dev-debug/gdb static server xml lzma -python -guile -source-highlight -nls

# gmp — unconditional gdb RDEPEND (arbitrary-precision value arithmetic
# since gdb ~13); pulled in automatically, no separate world entry needed
# (same pattern as cJSON/jansson/libmnl in prior batteries reports).
# static-libs is already on globally (make.conf USE=static-libs); asm and
# cpudetection are left at the global -* default (off) so gmp builds its
# portable C implementation rather than gambling on its i386 hand-tuned
# assembly paths against this exact musl/i486 cross toolchain — see report
# §3 for the reasoning.
dev-libs/gmp static-libs

# mpfr — unconditional gdb RDEPEND alongside gmp; static-libs propagates
# the same requirement onto gmp above, already satisfied.
dev-libs/mpfr static-libs

# expat — new dep, only pulled if gdb's xml USE is on (see above). -unicode
# overrides this repo's global USE=unicode (make.conf), which would
# otherwise make expat also build a redundant wide-char libexpatw.a that
# nothing in this image links against — see report §1.
dev-libs/expat static-libs -unicode

# strace - syscall tracer
dev-debug/strace static

# patch - apply diffs
sys-devel/patch static -nls

# wget - HTTP/FTP downloader with SSL
net-misc/wget static ssl -nls

# netcat
net-analyzer/netcat static

# whois
net-misc/whois static

# traceroute
net-analyzer/traceroute static

# iperf3 — SCTP support pulls in net-misc/lksctp-tools; not needed for the
# TCP/UDP bandwidth-testing use case and keeps the dependency set minimal.
net-misc/iperf -sctp

# mtr — combined ping+traceroute network diagnostic (My TraceRoute). ncurses
# UI (sys-libs/ncurses is already in world with tinfo+unicode — mtr-0.96-r1
# ships a Gentoo patch specifically for tinfo-split ncurses, see report).
# JSON output via jansson (new transitive dep — dev-libs/jansson, MIT,
# static-libs; see .batteries/reports/mtr.md §3). No GTK (-gui avoids
# pulling glib+gtk+:3).
# No file capabilities (-filecaps): raw sockets need root/CAP_NET_RAW, and
# this disc runs everything as root already, so fcaps.eclass's setcap step
# (and its sys-libs/libcap IDEPEND) is unneeded — same as this rootfs's
# existing no-cap posture elsewhere. filecaps also already defaults off
# under the global "USE=-*" reset; the line is kept for self-documentation
# matching this file's house style (e.g. the kmod/nethack entries above).
net-analyzer/mtr ncurses jansson -gui -filecaps

# net-tools - ifconfig, netstat, arp, route
sys-apps/net-tools static -nls

# ethtool — NIC driver/hardware control tool. Netlink interface via
# net-libs/libmnl (tiny, static-clean; Alpine ships a libmnl-static
# subpackage as direct evidence static linking is supported upstream).
# The ioctl fallback for old kernels/drivers stays compiled in regardless —
# netlink and ioctl are not mutually exclusive in this ebuild.
# No native IUSE=static on this ebuild (unlike net-tools/curl/wget); static
# linking here comes entirely from the repo-wide package.env static.conf
# catch-all (see configs/portage/package.env/cross-compile), same mechanism
# already relied on by hdparm/dmidecode/smartmontools/tcpdump/etc., which
# also carry no package.use/static entry of their own. "static" is included
# here only for documentation parity with dev-libs/openssl and
# dev-libs/libpcre2 above, which do the same despite lacking IUSE=static too.
sys-apps/ethtool static netlink

# libmnl — minimalistic netlink library (net-tools/nftables-adjacent code,
# now also pulled in by ethtool's netlink USE). New transitive dep; see
# .batteries/reports/ethtool.md §3. static-libs so ethtool links libmnl.a,
# not a .so this rootfs can't load.
net-libs/libmnl static static-libs

# tmux - terminal multiplexer
app-misc/tmux static -minimal

# htop - interactive process viewer
sys-process/htop static -minimal

# lsof - list open files
sys-process/lsof static

# sysklogd - syslog daemon
app-admin/sysklogd static

# dcron - minimal cron daemon
sys-process/dcron static

# e2fsprogs - ext2/3/4 tools (mkfs, fsck, tune2fs)
# tools USE flag builds static exes linked against libext2fs.so → linker error; drop it
sys-fs/e2fsprogs static static-libs -nls

# shadow - passwd, useradd, etc.; libsubid install location fixed via shadow-libdir.conf
sys-apps/shadow static -static-libs -pam -cracklib

# dosfstools - FAT filesystem tools (mkfs.fat, fsck.fat)
sys-fs/dosfstools static -nls

# squashfs-tools - mksquashfs, unsquashfs
sys-fs/squashfs-tools static

# lynx - text web browser with HTTPS
www-client/lynx static ssl -minimal -nls

# w3m - text web browser with HTTPS; disable image rendering (needs X)
www-client/w3m static ssl -minimal -imlib

# boehm-gc - conservative GC; new dep of www-client/w3m. static-libs is a
# real IUSE flag here (unlike w3m's own -minimal/-static no-ops) — the
# global static-libs USE already flips it on via multilib_src_configure's
# use_enable, this line documents that intent explicitly.
dev-libs/boehm-gc static-libs

# libatomic_ops - new transitive dep of boehm-gc. No static/static-libs
# IUSE on this ebuild at all (see report §1) — its multilib_src_configure
# hardcodes '--enable-shared'; relying on EXTRA_ECONF's trailing
# --disable-shared (from the repo-wide static.conf catch-all) to win via
# configure's last-flag-wins behavior, same mechanism as every other
# no-native-IUSE=static package in this tree (hdparm, dmidecode, ethtool).
# Line kept for documentation parity even though there's nothing to toggle.
dev-libs/libatomic_ops static

# mutt - email client. REQUIRED_USE: imap? (ssl); smtp? (ssl sasl);
# gsasl? (sasl). ssl uses openssl (already in world) over gnutls to avoid
# a second TLS stack. imap+smtp cover read+send; hcache/gpgme/idn/kerberos/
# doc/autocrypt/slang left at the global -* default (see report §2 for why
# each is skippable) — this rootfs ships no local MTA, so smtp is what makes
# *sending* mail work at all, not an optional extra.
#
# sasl backend: gsasl, not the default cyrus-sasl. cyrus-sasl inherits
# tmpfiles.eclass -> RDEPEND=virtual/tmpfiles -> (USE=-systemd here) ->
# sys-apps/systemd-utils[tmpfiles], which is a Python (python-single-r1)
# package this build has no interest in cross-compiling. The only other
# virtual/tmpfiles provider, sys-apps/seedfiles, exists in ::gentoo only as
# a keywordless -9999 live ebuild, which this repo's ACCEPT_KEYWORDS="*"
# explicitly excludes (see make.conf) -- so gsasl is the clean path, not a
# workaround. See .batteries/reports/mutt.md §2-3.
mail-client/mutt static ssl imap smtp sasl gsasl -gpgme -autocrypt -idn -kerberos -hcache -doc -debug -slang -nls

# gsasl - SASL library backing mutt's smtp+sasl support above. New
# transitive dep (net-misc/gsasl); see .batteries/reports/mutt.md §3.
# +client +server are REQUIRED_USE'd (|| ( client server )) but global -*
# would zero both -- client is the only one mutt (a SASL client, never a
# server) actually needs; -server keeps the build to the minimum mechanism
# set. gcrypt/gnutls/idn/kerberos/nls/ntlm all left off: none of mutt's
# SASL auth mechanisms (PLAIN/LOGIN/CRAM-MD5/DIGEST-MD5, negotiated over
# the already-TLS-secured IMAP/SMTP connection) need them, and leaving them
# off keeps gsasl's only real dependency at sys-libs/readline (already
# static, already in world).
net-misc/gsasl static-libs client -server

# irssi - IRC client with SSL
net-irc/irssi static ssl -minimal -otr -socks -nls

# figlet - ASCII art text banners
app-misc/figlet static

# fortune-mod - random fortune cookies
games-misc/fortune-mod -nls

# cmatrix - terminal matrix rain animation
app-misc/cmatrix static

# sl - steam locomotive (typo correction for ls)
app-misc/sl static

# gpm - console mouse daemon
app-misc/gpm static

# nethack - curses roguelike; ncurses UI is unconditional in 3.6.x (no USE
# flag gates it — only X11 is togglable). No qt/gtk/minimal IUSE exists on
# this package; keep the atom minimal rather than setting no-op flags.
games-roguelike/nethack -X
